description: Use PRs for medium and large changes
alwaysApply: true
---

# Pull requests

- **Medium or large** changes (multi-file features, security fixes, API/auth behavior, engine changes, breaking changes) must use a feature branch and a **GitHub pull request** — not direct commits to `main`.
- Default integration branch: **`dev`** → PR into **`main`** unless specified otherwise.
- PR description must include **Summary**, **Test plan** (commands run), and a pointer to **CHANGELOG** `[Unreleased]`.
- Small one-line fixes may commit to `dev` without a PR only when explicitly requested; when in doubt, open a PR.
